   "text": "I read the structure in pieces and wrote each piece out in turn.\n\n**Left end:** a benzothiophene-2-carboxamide with a CF2\u2013PO3H2 group at C5 of the benzo ring.\n\n**Bicyclic core:** an 8-membered ring fused to a pyrrolidine through the pyrrolidine N and one pyrrolidine carbon. The 8-membered ring runs N(CH2CHF2)\u2013CH2\u2013CH(NH-acyl)\u2013C(=O)\u2013N(pyrrolidine)\u2013CH(fusion)\u2013CH2\u2013CH2. The pyrrolidine carbon next to its N carries the C(=O)NH link to the next residue.\n\n**Peptide chain:** Gln (side chain CH2CH2C(=O)NH2), then 4-tert-butyl-Phe, whose C=O forms an amide with a piperidine N.\n\n**Linker and right end:** the piperidine is substituted at C4 by a (CH2)3 chain ending in NH. That NH is attached to C4 of an isoindolinone, and the isoindolinone N is attached to a 2,6-dioxopiperidin-3-yl ring.\n\n**Stereocentres:** I assigned CIP descriptors from the drawn wedges and then chose the SMILES symbols to match.\n- The CH bearing NH-acyl is S.\n- The ring-fusion carbon is R.\n- The pyrrolidine carbon bearing the C(=O)NH is S.\n- Gln is S and the tBu-Phe \u03b1-carbon is S (both L-amino acids).\n- The glutarimide carbon has plain bonds in the drawing, so I left it unspecified.\n\nSMILES: O=C(N[C@H]1CN(CC(F)F)CC[C@H]2CC[C@@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc3ccc(C(C)(C)C)cc3)C(=O)N3CCC(CCCNc4cccc5c4CN(C5=O)C4CCC(=O)NC4=O)CC3)N2C1=O)c1cc2cc(C(F)(F)P(=O)(O)O)ccc2s1"
